]=14.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-2Y]={(1)}^{2}\\cdot 16+{(-2)}^{2}\\cdot 14=72.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0df88138-7309-5a09-9a96-5e26029f0186" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Raw Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "470fe4ad-51df-50c6-83d4-4d686c35f255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,266" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427773} {:answer/id #uuid "523e03e2-f365-5567-ab98-1e025821379c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,658" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427778} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba0063e-a975-5758-994c-986c4758ed5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,568" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427784} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c001b0-8ead-529a-a5b2-aa514dabdc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,622" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427809} {:answer/id #uuid "d80cdd5f-bead-5687-94fb-296a1beafec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,842" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ba0063e-a975-5758-994c-986c4758ed5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,568" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427784} :answer-field/id #uuid "d64db08b-4f84-5e15-8525-c73d14e5127f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa8e6a54-051a-56fa-aeb3-ee00c8a84aa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-109974" :question/problem "Consider two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=37,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=25$\nand second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=1\\,401$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=705.$ Find the variance of  $3X+4Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,401-{37}^{2} \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =705-{25}^{2} \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X+4Y] & ={3}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{4}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =9(32)+16(80) \\\\  & =1\\,568.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0df88138-7309-5a09-9a96-5e26029f0186" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Raw Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f021fc-cc2d-56e3-8549-9018e92500b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427759} {:answer/id #uuid "358e6ed1-456d-5c31-b522-5dd2e300185b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427768} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae52d7c-80f7-51dc-b5e0-1d93eab04f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.01" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427776} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec41a73-b969-5f1b-891e-cb6ce24c4326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.71" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427790} {:answer/id #uuid "bb73c5e2-f1c0-53dd-9d7c-8cba38f9f362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ec41a73-b969-5f1b-891e-cb6ce24c4326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.71" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427790} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fc7e634-9241-5da2-bb25-fa1fb32a0da9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "126f21c0-348e-55fb-ab07-2260eac6b3ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-109976" :question/problem "Consider two independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=18,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=21$\nand second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=380$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=460.$ Find the variance of  $0.5X-0.3Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =380-{18}^{2} \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =460-{21}^{2} \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[0.5X-0.3Y] & ={0.5}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+(-0.3)^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =0.25(56.0)+0.09(19.0) \\\\  & =15.71.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0df88138-7309-5a09-9a96-5e26029f0186" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Raw Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16da9045-3774-565d-8722-b9399fd55b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427758} {:answer/id #uuid "47b12922-191d-51cc-b22f-5dbac48b2f5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427774} {:answer/id #uuid "a3183d04-1de5-5da0-a92a-526796a91f9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.93" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427797} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7be552-98bb-5949-9c86-86c25f6786c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427805} {:answer/id #uuid "c048cea2-997e-5b85-86aa-515e658212f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c048cea2-997e-5b85-86aa-515e658212f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427807} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa63e5b7-4ca2-5180-96bb-3d2473b05bc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbe4a1cf-3a7c-53c0-adbf-9f73e68e01a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-109984" :question/problem "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n Find $\\text{Var}[5X-0.5Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.25+0\\cdot 0.25+1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.25+0\\cdot 0.25+1\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.75-{0.25}^{2} \\\\  & =0.6875.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =10\\cdot 0.1+11\\cdot 0.7+12\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =11.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =100\\cdot 0.1+121\\cdot 0.7+144\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =123.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =123.5-{11.1}^{2} \\\\  & =0.29.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[5X-0.5Y] & ={5}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+(-0.5)^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =25(0.6875)+0.25(0.29) \\\\  & =17.26.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162067 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0df88138-7309-5a09-9a96-5e26029f0186" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Combined Variance Given Some Raw Moments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1526fbe8-b614-5f14-bbfe-58ab3d68130d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22.63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427757} {:answer/id #uuid "59ecf085-ff6f-5dcc-9f47-c9a5c9084a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427782} {:answer/id #uuid "6b61665f-a1ca-5dc7-a4b8-e91ab4670044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427783} {:answer/id #uuid "b96a1a92-a624-54d0-8f80-5c92e194e09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427803} {:answer/id #uuid "f3011c3c-c886-51b9-97ac-772039732c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b61665f-a1ca-5dc7-a4b8-e91ab4670044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427783} :answer-field/id #uuid "e74e953e-0c9f-5bc1-88b6-b8760660b58b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1cad1397-85fb-5493-b4be-5ce5c5dffe60" :question/math-academy-id "q-109987" :question/problem "The probability mass function of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.34$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.52$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.14$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n Find $\\text{Var}[2X+7Y].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of $X$ is determined by the formula \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.34+0\\cdot 0.52+1\\cdot 0.14 \\\\  & =-0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.34+0\\cdot 0.52+1\\cdot 0.14 \\\\  & =0.48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.48-(-0.2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y}$, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 0.15+6\\cdot 0.6+7\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =6.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot f(y) \\\\  & =25\\cdot 0.15+36\\cdot 0.6+49\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =37.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =37.6-{6.1}^{2} \\\\  & =0.39.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X+7Y] & ={2}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{7}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y] \\\\  & =4(0.44)+49(0.39) \\\\  & =20.87.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162068 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e3dad37-612c-56f1-a571-360fafe336b4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Variance of a Sum or Difference of Independent Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c71cac7-4ef8-5b19-9e0f-fed180f37fb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158979} {:answer/id #uuid "9ddf2406-24aa-5003-b8c5-ac0d53e393d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/va